      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALOHA BLUE (1) hasn't broken through for an extended period but has been catching the eye with some strong closing efforts. Will likely get back again from the wide draw and be flashing hard late. BRISEIS ECLIPSE (2) showed good tactical speed fresh but just lacked fitness late on a wet Murray Bridge track. Better for that and will prove tougher to reel in this time if they roll forward again. SHE SPARKLES (10) was better second-up when settling in a handy spot closer to the speed, only beaten a long neck here. Was slow to recover last time but backs up quickly a week late. Drawn well and looks a genuine winning hope. LUNARSHOT (5) got the job done third-up when settling closer to the action. Suspect they look to be handy again from the inside draw. In the mix.",
